    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump\n\n### Description\n\nThis feature request is based on [this](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2303#issuecomment-4078015984) comment\n\n-- edited --\n\nScenario with file containing a single word:\n\n> mark\n\n- Open file, position cursor on the 'a'\n- Type `dfm`\n- Notice that text is not modified, as expected\n- Notice that m is *not* highlighted\n\nNotably, highlighting does work as expected using the same scenario with different file contents: Empty first line, mark is on the second with cursor on its a\n\n\n\n",
