            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> This restores highlighting in both directions for the given scenario. All tests pass.\n\nThis feels better, although still relies on the fact that \"consuming character\" will trigger `CursorMoved`.\n\nI'd like to spend again some more time to maybe find a fundamentally better approach than the one that require `undo!`. Because there are other issues with it which you haven't found yet :) Like when doing `dfm` on an empty line.",
